pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:short_dry_grass=Short Dry Grass is a sparse, brittle patch of grass found in §6Deserts§r and §6Badlands§r. It adds a realistic, parched aesthetic to dry landscapes and can be harvested with §7Shears§r for decoration.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:tall_dry_grass=Tall Dry Grass is a dried-out variant of grass that grows in §6Dry§r and §6Desert-like§r environments. It can be sheared for decorative use and contributes to the wild, untamed look of the terrain.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:bush=Bushes are small, leafy green plants that grow across various §aOverworld§r biomes. They provide subtle ground cover and are often used to enhance natural-looking terrain and forested builds.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:firefly_bush=The Firefly Bush is a glowing shrub found in select §aOverworld§r biomes. It emits soft light and occasionally releases §eFireflies§r at night, making it a magical decorative element in gardens and forests.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:cactus_flower=Cactus Flowers bloom atop §2Cacti§r in §6Desert§r biomes. These vibrant blossoms offer a splash of color to the arid landscape and can be collected with §7Shears§r for decoration or dye crafting.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:leaf_litter=Leaf Litter is a natural ground covering composed of fallen leaves, commonly found beneath §aTrees§r in forested biomes. It enhances forest floor detail and is often used in natural path designs.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:windflowers=Windflowers are delicate blossoms that sway gently in the breeze. Found in open §aPlains§r and §aMeadows§r, they are perfect for serene gardens and decorative landscapes.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:short_grass=Short Grass is a simple patch of §2grass§r that can be found in most §aOverworld§r biomes. It serves as a common decorative ground cover and can be obtained using §7Shears§r. Breaking it without shears may yield §aSeeds§r, making it useful for farming.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:fern=The Fern is a small green plant that thrives in §aTaiga§r and §aOld Growth Spruce Taiga§r biomes. It can be harvested with §7Shears§r and is often used for §adecorative landscaping§r, adding a natural feel to forests and gardens.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:tall_grass=Tall Grass is a longer variant of regular grass, appearing in many §aOverworld§r biomes, especially plains. When broken, it has a chance to drop §aSeeds§r, making it a helpful source for early-game wheat farming. It can also be obtained with §7Shears§r for decorative use.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:large_fern=Large Ferns are taller versions of §2Ferns§r, naturally found in §aTaiga§r and §aOld Growth Taiga§r biomes. They can be collected using §7Shears§r and make excellent decorations for forested areas, blending well with other vegetation.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:dandelion=The Dandelion is a bright yellow flower that naturally spawns in most grassy biomes of the §aOverworld§r. It can be crafted into §eYellow Dye§r, making it useful for coloring wool, banners, and other items. Dandelions are also used as food for rabbits.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:poppy=Poppies are red flowers commonly found in various biomes. They are also dropped by defeated §cIron Golems§r. This flower can be crafted into §cRed Dye§r, used in a variety of decorative applications.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:red_tulip=The Red Tulip is a vibrant red flower that naturally appears in §aFlower Forests§r and plains biomes. It can be converted into §cRed Dye§r and is often used in decorative gardens due to its bright appearance.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pink_tulip=The Pink Tulip is a delicate and beautiful flower found in §aFlower Forests§r. It can be crafted into §dPink Dye§r, making it a valuable resource for coloring wool and other materials.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:white_tulip=The White Tulip is a pure, elegant flower that grows in §aFlower Forests§r. It can be converted into §fWhite Dye§r, making it useful for lightening or recoloring other dyes.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:orange_tulip=The Orange Tulip is a bright and cheerful flower found in §aFlower Forests§r. It can be crafted into §6Orange Dye§r, useful for various decorative purposes.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:allium=Alliums are rare purple flowers that spawn naturally in §aFlower Forests§r. They can be crafted into §dPurple Dye§r and make a great decorative addition to gardens and builds.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:lily_of_the_valley=Lily of the Valley is an elegant white flower that grows in §aFlower Forests§r. When crafted, it produces §fWhite Dye§r. This flower is known for its delicate appearance, making it a favorite for decorative gardens.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:blue_orchid=Thanks to its light blue petals, the Blue Orchid is a flower that really sticks out from others in Minecraft. The Blue Orchid can exclusively be found in the §qSwamp§r biome, or besides that can be purchased from §eWandering Traders§r. It can be crafted into §blight blue dye§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:oxeye_daisy=The Oxeye Daisy is a white flower with a yellow center, found in grassy biomes. It can be crafted into §fLight Gray Dye§r and is often used as a symbol of peace and beauty in builds.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:cornflower=Cornflowers are striking blue flowers that generate naturally in plains and flower forests. They can be crafted into §9Blue Dye§r, making them a valuable resource for colorful builds.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:azure_bluet=Azure Bluets are small, pale flowers found in grassy biomes. They can be crafted into §7Light Gray Dye§r and are commonly used in natural landscaping due to their subtle color.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pink_petals=Pink Petals are clusters of soft pink flowers that spread across the ground, naturally spawning in the §dCherry Grove§r biome. They can be placed in various formations, making them ideal for detailed garden designs.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:deadbush=Dead Bushes are dried, lifeless plants found in §6Deserts§r and §6Badlands§r. They drop sticks when broken, unless harvested with §7Shears§r, in which case they can be collected for decorative purposes.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:bamboo=Bamboo is a rapidly growing plant that thrives in §aBamboo Jungles§r. It can be used to craft §9Scaffolding§r, serve as fuel, or be used to breed pandas. Bamboo is also a key material in making sticks efficiently.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:reeds=Reeds, more commonly known as §aSugar Cane§r, grow near water sources in many biomes. They are harvested to craft §ePaper§r and §eSugar§r, both of which are essential in crafting books and potions.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:wither_rose=The Wither Rose is a rare, dark flower that is dropped when a mob is killed by a §7Wither§r. It inflicts the §cWither§r effect on any entity that comes into contact with it. The flower can be crafted into §7Black Dye§r and is often used in traps or ominous builds.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:lilac=The Lilac is a tall, two-block purple flower commonly found in grassy biomes. It can be converted into §dMagenta Dye§r and adds a touch of elegance to gardens.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:rose_bush=Rose Bushes are clusters of vibrant red roses growing in grassy biomes. They can be used to craft §cRed Dye§r and make any garden look more lively.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:peony=The Peony is a large pink flowering bush that generates naturally in grassy biomes. It can be crafted into §dPink Dye§r, making it a valuable decorative plant.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:sunflower=The Sunflower is a tall, bright yellow flower that always faces east. It naturally spawns in §aSunflower Plains§r and can be crafted into §6Yellow Dye§r. Due to its unique directionality, it can be used as a natural compass.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:torchflower=The Torchflower is an ancient-looking plant with a fiery orange hue. It is exclusively grown from §eTorchflower Seeds§r, which can be obtained by brushing §6Suspicious Sand§r in §aDesert Temples§r. It can be crafted into §6Orange Dye§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pitcher_plant=The Pitcher Plant is a unique, tall flower that originates from §ePitcher Pods§r found in §6Suspicious Sand§r within §aDesert Temples§r. It can be grown and harvested for decoration or to craft §2Green Dye§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:small_dripleaf_block=Small Dripleaf is a short aquatic plant that generates in §aLush Caves§r. When placed in water or moist environments, it can grow into a §aBig Dripleaf§r, which has interactive movement properties.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:big_dripleaf=Big Dripleaf is a unique, interactive plant from §aLush Caves§r. When stood on, its leaves tilt, temporarily dropping players. It is commonly used for parkour and decorative builds.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:azalea=The Azalea is a small, leafy shrub found near §aLush Caves§r. It indicates the presence of an underground §aLush Cave§r and can be grown into an §aAzalea Tree§r when placed on dirt and given §bBone Meal§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:flowering_azalea=The Flowering Azalea is a variant of the §aAzalea§r that blooms with purple flowers. It naturally generates above §aLush Caves§r and serves as a decorative block for gardens and landscapes.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:torchflower_crop=The Torchflower Crop is the growing stage of the §6Torchflower§r. It must be planted using §eTorchflower Seeds§r and will mature into a fully grown flower over time.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pitcher_crop=The Pitcher Crop is the early growth stage of the §2Pitcher Plant§r. It starts as a small sprout and matures into a tall flower when planted from §ePitcher Pods§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:wheat=Wheat is a staple crop that can be grown from §aSeeds§r. It is used to craft §eBread§r, breed livestock, and create §6Hay Bales§r for storage or decoration.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:carrots=Carrots are orange root vegetables that can be farmed and eaten. They are essential for breeding §dPigs§r and crafting §6Golden Carrots§r, which are used for potions and high-tier food.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:potatoes=Potatoes are versatile crops that can be farmed and cooked into §6Baked Potatoes§r, offering better hunger restoration. They may also drop as §cPoisonous Potatoes§r, which have limited uses.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:beetroot=Beetroots are red crops that grow from §aBeetroot Seeds§r. They can be used to make §cBeetroot Soup§r and can be crafted into §cRed Dye§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:melon_stem=Melon Stems grow from §aMelon Seeds§r and, once matured, produce juicy §2Melons§r, which can be eaten or crafted into §eGlistering Melons§r for brewing.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pumpkin_stem=Pumpkin Stems grow from §aPumpkin Seeds§r and, when mature, yield §6Pumpkins§r, useful for crafting Jack o'Lanterns, Pumpkin Pie, or carved decorations.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:sweet_berry_bush=Sweet Berry Bushes generate naturally in §aTaiga§r biomes. They provide §cSweet Berries§r, which can be eaten or used to breed §dFoxes§r. Walking through a bush causes slight damage.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:oak_sapling=Oak Saplings grow into §aOak Trees§r when placed on dirt and given §bBone Meal§r. They are one of the most common tree types in the game.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:birch_sapling=Birch Saplings grow into §aBirch Trees§r, recognized by their white bark. They are commonly found in §aBirch Forests§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:spruce_sapling=Spruce Saplings grow into §aSpruce Trees§r, which are common in §aTaiga§r biomes. They can grow into massive trees when placed in a 2x2 arrangement.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:acacia_sapling=Acacia Saplings grow into §aAcacia Trees§r, which are distinct for their diagonal trunks and spawn in §aSavannas§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:cherry_sapling=Cherry Saplings grow into §dCherry Trees§r, which produce pink leaves and wood. They are exclusive to the §dCherry Grove§r biome.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:jungle_sapling=Jungle Saplings grow into §aJungle Trees§r, which are tall and thick. When planted in a 2x2 square, they can form massive trees.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:dark_oak_sapling=Dark Oak Saplings require four saplings to grow into a §aDark Oak Tree§r, found in §aDark Forests§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pale_oak_sapling=Pale Oak Saplings grow into §aPale Oak Trees§r, a special variation of the common oak tree.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:red_mushroom=Red Mushrooms are found in dark areas and §cMushroom Fields§r. They can be used to craft §cMushroom Stew§r or grown into giant mushrooms.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:brown_mushroom=Brown Mushrooms generate in dark places and §cMushroom Fields§r. They are used for §cMushroom Stew§r and brewing §cWeakness Potions§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:waterlily=Water Lilies float on the surface of water and are commonly found in §qSwamps§r. They can be used for decoration and walking paths.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:seagrass=Seagrass is an underwater plant found in §bOceans§r and §bRivers§r. It can be harvested for breeding §dTurtles§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:sea_pickle=Sea Pickles emit light underwater and are found in §bWarm Oceans§r. They can be used as decoration or smelted into §dLime Dye§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:kelp=Kelp is an aquatic plant growing in §bOceans§r. When dried, it becomes a renewable fuel source.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:pale_hanging_moss=Pale Hanging Moss is a decorative plant found in §aLush Caves§r, adding to their vibrant underground aesthetic.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:glow_lichen=Glow Lichen is a dim light source found in caves. It can be harvested with §7Shears§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:spore_blossom=Spore Blossoms are large pink flowers hanging from cave ceilings in §aLush Caves§r, releasing particles for ambiance.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:chorus_flower=Chorus Flowers grow on §5Chorus Plants§r in the §5End§r and are necessary for cultivating more chorus trees.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:closed_eyeblossom=The Closed Eyeblossom is a mysterious plant found in the pale garden biome. It remains shut, watching its surroundings with an eerie presence.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:open_eyeblossom=The Open Eyeblossom is an awakened version of the §5Closed Eyeblossom§r, seemingly observing everything nearby. It thrives in deep, shadowy environments.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:hanging_roots=Hanging Roots are delicate plants found beneath §aAzalea Trees§r, adding realism to cave ceilings.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:warped_roots=Warped Roots are small, twisted plants native to the §3Warped Forest§r. They serve as decorative blocks and can be composted for bone meal.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:crimson_roots=Crimson Roots are strange, red vegetation found in the §cCrimson Forest§r. They can be harvested for decoration or used as a composting ingredient.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:nether_sprouts=Nether Sprouts are small, blue-green plants found in the §3Warped Forest§r. They add to the eerie atmosphere of the Nether's biomes.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:warped_fungus=Warped Fungus is a strange, blue mushroom growing in the §3Warped Forest§r. It repels §cHoglins§r and is used to breed and control §3Striders§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:crimson_fungus=Crimson Fungus is a red mushroom native to the §cCrimson Forest§r. It is essential for breeding §cHoglins§r and can be grown into giant §cCrimson Trees§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:vine=Vines are climbable plants that grow on trees and walls, often found in §aJungles§r and §qSwamps§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:cave_vines=Cave Vines are luminescent, hanging plants found in §aLush Caves§r. They can grow Glow Berries, which serve as both a food source and a natural light source.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:twisting_vines=Twisting Vines are climbable plants found in the §3Warped Forest§r. Unlike regular vines, they grow upwards and can be used for vertical traversal.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.minecraft:weeping_vines=Weeping Vines are red, hanging plants native to the §cCrimson Forest§r. They grow downward from the Nether's ceilings and are useful for climbing.
