tile.pod_gard:bergenia.name=Bergenia
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:bergenia=The Bergenia's large leathery leaves are often tinged a glossy red in winter, complementing the warm pale rose color of the petals. The riot of colors draws tinters to the wilds of the §2forest and flower forests§r, who seek to exploit the flower's warm color in their §dpink dyes§r.
tile.pod_gard:bird_of_paradise.name=Bird Of Paradise
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:bird_of_paradise=The exotic Bird of Paradise is a tough plant that thrives in the rugged and savage §2jungle§r. Many legends find their origin in the unique and brightly colored flowers that resemble the head of a bird. Some say the §yellow dye§r it produces has magical properties, while others scoff at such superstition.
tile.pod_gard:bluebell.name=Bluebell
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:bluebell=The §2flower forests§r host a multitude of bluebells, which emerge in droves to carpet the woodlands with a riot of deep, dark blue tones. The radiance they give to the §2forests§r they inhabit are often replicated in clothes thanks to the charming §1blue dye§r it can produce.
