pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:red_buttercup=The Red Buttercup can grow so dense that it forms scarlet meadows that dazzle any who travel to the sweeping §aplains§r, §ameadows§r, and §asunflower plains§r. Nobles and other aristocrats have become fond of clothes that use the §4red dye§r procured from the flowers' sanguine tint.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:white_buttercup=The White Buttercup can grow so dense that it forms sweeping meadows that dazzle any who travel to the §aplains§r, §ameadows§r, and §asunflower plains§r.
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:yellow_buttercup=The Yellow Buttercup can grow so dense that it forms sweeping meadows that dazzle any who travel to the §aplains§r, §ameadows§r, and §asunflower plains§r. Villagers and farmers have grown fond of clothes that use the §eyellow dye§r procured from the flowers' sunshine tint.
tile.pod_gard:butterfly_bush.name=Butterfly Bush
pod_gard.lexicon.plant.pod_gard:butterfly_bush=The butterfly bush is a favorite nectar source for butterflies and emits a delightful honey scent. They dot the most remote of §qswamps§r and, with careful prepaeration, can create a vivid §dpink dye§r.
